      "code": "QUESTION_LEVEL_ABSTENTION",
      "evidence": "No complete question candidate was produced. One option was classified SELECTED in the second document, but other uncertain options prevented a question candidate.",
      "interpretation": "An option decision is not a correctly answered question; accuracy requires independent truth comparison."
    },
    {
      "code": "SMALL_FITTED_CHECKBOX",
      "evidence": "All 38 checkbox option crops in the first document were 27-28 pixels per side; fitted printed-box widths were 10-12 pixels, below the production 14-pixel minimum.",
      "interpretation": "Outer ROI size passed the 20-pixel guard. This is fitted-border scale/localization failure, not missing manual regions."
    },
    {
      "code": "PRINTED_CORE_EDGE_INK",
      "evidence": "116 first-document and 88 second-document circle options reported PRINTED_CORE_UNRELIABLE. First-document cores had at least 27 ink pixels, with edge ink 3-28 pixels in cores approximately 14-15 by 19-21 pixels.",
      "interpretation": "These first-document rejections are caused by ink touching the printed-core boundary, not empty or unconfirmed cores."
    },
    {
      "code": "REAL_SCAN_OPTION_GUARDS",
      "evidence": "Across both inputs, OPTION_TOO_BLURRED occurred 53 times and CIRCLE_OR_INK_CROPPED 94 times; the second input also had 7 PRINTED_CORE_TOO_LARGE decisions.",
      "interpretation": "Frozen grayscale, boundary and core-geometry guards withheld candidates. Measurements are diagnostic values, not accuracy."
    },
    {
      "code": "ALIGNMENT_LIMIT",
      "evidence": "First input: five pages ALIGNED and one FAILED with MATCHES_TOO_LOCAL. Second input: seven ALIGNED and one NOT_REQUIRED because all targets on that page were manual.",
      "interpretation": "Even the same-source calibration run did not pass every automatic alignment gate."
    },
    {
      "code": "SCALAR_AND_MANUAL_LIMITS",
      "evidence": "Scalar observations included six NO_READABLE_TEXT, one INVALID_NUMBER, two INVALID_DATE and one BASE_ENHANCED_OCR_CONFLICT. Forty-five text targets and four manually configured choice targets required human input.",
      "interpretation": "Manual fields are intentional abstentions, and no human values were credited as machine output."
    },
    {
      "code": "NATIVE_PROCESS_LIFECYCLE_FAILURE",
      "evidence": "Both recognition jobs reached READY and wrote raw-report digests, followed by the same failing native test-process exit.",
      "interpretation": "The saved candidate measurement exists, but the end-to-end native process test did not pass. The responsible native module and fault phase are unverified."
    },
    {
      "code": "CHINESE_VERTICAL_MODEL_DEPENDENCY",
      "evidence": "The bundled Chinese traineddata configurations request corresponding vertical sublanguages that are absent from the current bundled model inventory; the Chinese run emitted a missing-sublanguage warning.",
      "interpretation": "The startup availability check covers the primary three model files only. The warning alone does not establish total OCR failure or the native crash cause."
    }
